This PR added supports for `extract.extractors` options for `windi.config.js` which should be compatible with PurgeCSS's extractors

```ts
// windi.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from 'windicss/helpers'

export default defineConfig({
  extract: {
    extractors: [{
      extensions: ['md', 'mdx']
      extractor(code) {
        /* ... */
      },
    }]
  }
})
```

And moving the `pug` support from the transformer to a built-in extractor. It will enable on demand as previously, the existing apps should work the same and there are no migrations needed.

### @windicss/plugin-tuils

#### Breaking Change

- `utils.extractFile()` is now **async**

In addition to bind:selected approach I'd like to have "change" event that fires within the pick function.
```
<script>
  import Datepicker from "praecox-datepicker";

  let current_date;

  const handleChangeDate = e => current_date = new Date(e.detail);

  $: console.log(current_date)

</script>

<Datepicker on:change={ handleChangeDate } />
```

## Evaluation criteria

* [x] - All data fetches done as actions and received from store by components; 
* [x] - Creating, editing, deleting and updating (CRUD operations) of films are done as redux actions; 
* [x] - Sorting by release date and rating done as redux actions;  
* [x] - Filtering by genre is done as redux actions.

## Overview
Closes #84 

Uses react-big-calendar. 

**Note: will be adding more styling later, priority was getting calendar component working**
**Note:  Unfortunately [react-big-calendar](https://github.com/jquense/react-big-calendar#localization-and-date-formatting) only uses `Globalize.js`, `date-fns`, or `Moment.js`, so this results in some tech debt since we already use `Dayjs`**

<img width="1439" alt="Screen Shot 2021-04-27 at 11 42 18 PM" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/31324580/116359232-6dea7a80-a7b3-11eb-80ee-410cb23dafe3.png">

`ScheduleCalendar` takes a list of the custom interface `CalendarEvent`, which is information about the section + colour of the event to be put on the calendar.

To create recurring events I used RRule, which generates the events using the start date and some specified params, like week, intervals, etc..

### Misc Info

Behaviour of the calendar:
- When no events -> goes to current day
- When there is an event -> goes to min event date

Some nice things to know are in `SchedulerCalendar`:
- `eventStyleGetter` styles the whole event
- `CustomEvent` is the react component that goes within the event that displays all info about the event.

In the future, it is possible for onClicks on events, but that should be a separate ticket.

### Testing to see events

Replace `pages > scheduler > scheduler.tsx` with this
```
import { Flex } from '@chakra-ui/layout';

import { Header, SchedulerContainer } from '../../app';
import { useSections } from '../../shared/fetchers';

export function Scheduler(): JSX.Element {
  const term = '202105';
  const subject = 'ECE';
  const code = '310';
  const { data: scehdulelisting } = useSections({ term, queryParams: { subject, code } });
  return (
    <Flex h="100vh" direction="column">
      <Header />
      {scehdulelisting && (
        <SchedulerContainer
          calendarEvents={(() => {
            const x = new Array();
            x.push({
              subject: subject,
              code: code,
              color: 'green',
              sectionCode: scehdulelisting[0].sectionCode,
              meetingTime: scehdulelisting[0].meetingTimes[0],
            });
            return x;
          })()}
        />
      )}
    </Flex>
  );
}

```
